wed the preprocessing exactly as described in Appendix F (100→200 Hz, 0.1-75 Hz bandpass, 50 Hz notch, removed EOG, 2s windows / 50ms stride, 10min/5min/5min split, ÷90 normalization, all 8 subjects). Fine-tuning hyperparameters are identical to the paper's Table 5. Tried both center and end-of-window alignment for joint labels, tried both scipy and MNE filtering — results barely changed. Would really appreciate any tips if you managed to get closer to the reported numbers, or if you'd be willing to compare notes.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/935963004/LaBraM/issues/comments/4720206363/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]